course: dictionary
lesson: 3213
title: Enlist: join up or ask for help
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Enlist can mean to join the army, navy or air force. It can also mean to ask someone to help you and get them to agree. Context tells you which meaning is in use.
explain: «We enlisted Dad to carry the boxes» does not mean Dad joined the army. Swap in the meaning «we asked Dad to help us carry the boxes» and the sentence still makes sense, so this is the help meaning.
explain: In history, «many young men enlisted» means they joined the army, and some lied about their age to do it. The words around enlisted, such as young men and army, are the clues. Watch for the phrases «enlist in the army» and «enlist the help of».
fact: Enlist is a verb: enlist, enlists, enlisted, enlisting.
fact: «Enlist in the army» means to join the army, navy or air force.
fact: «Enlist the help of» someone means to ask them to help you and get them to agree.
fact: An anagram is a word made by rearranging all the letters of another word.
fact: «Listen», «silent», «tinsel» and «enlist» are anagrams: they use the same letters in a different order.
exercise: «We enlisted Dad to carry the boxes.» What does enlisted mean here? | *Asked him to help and got him to agree | Sent him to the shops | Joined the army | Put his name on a list
exercise: In the First World War, many young men «enlisted» in the army. What does enlisted mean? | Wrote letters home | Left school early | Went on holiday | *Joined the army
exercise: The anagram example says «enlist» is made from the letters of «listen». Which word is also an anagram of «listen»? | Lessen | Listing | *Silent | Listed
test: In «They enlisted the help of the teacher», what does enlisted the help of mean? | Made a list of all the teachers | Stopped the teacher from helping | *Got the teacher to agree to help | Thanked the teacher loudly
test: Which word fits the gap? «Last year, Sam ___ in the navy.» | enlist | enlists | *enlisted | enlisting
exam: Which list gives the correct forms of the verb enlist? | *enlist, enlists, enlisted, enlisting | enlisted, enlisting, enlisted, enlists | enlist, enlisted, enlists, listen | enlisting, enlists, enlister, enlist
